{
  "sections": {
    "opening": {
      "type": "ca-ai-opening",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "AI business intelligence and consulting for eCommerce brands",
        "heading": "A Brain for your business.",
        "text": "One memory for everything your team, your store, your code and your marketing platforms know. An all-knowing AI for your business.",
        "enter_sound_label": "Enter with sound",
        "enter_silent_label": "Enter without sound",
        "scroll_label": "Scroll",
        "sound_on_label": "Sound on",
        "sound_off_label": "Sound off",
        "audio_url": "",
        "example_label": "Example",
        "auto_on_label": "Autoplay on",
        "auto_off_label": "Autoplay off"
      }
    },
    "brain": {
      "type": "ca-ai-chapter",
      "blocks": {
        "act_1": {
          "type": "act",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Your AI can't answer what it can't see.",
            "text": "<p>The answers are in a Slack thread, a release, an ad account and last week's call. Your AI sees none of them.</p>",
            "length": 150
          }
        },
        "act_2": {
          "type": "act",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Adding more sources doesn't help either.",
            "text": "<p>Connecting all your data is a start. But now every question means reading all of it, which is slow, and the few records that matter are buried in the noise.</p>",
            "length": 150
          }
        },
        "act_3": {
          "type": "act",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "The Brain's neural network gets straight to the answer.",
            "text": "<p>It jumps intelligently between records from different sources to gather the right context, then gives one answer with its sources.</p>",
            "length": 150
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "act_1",
        "act_2",
        "act_3"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "variant": "brain",
        "number": "01",
        "chapter": "The Business Brain"
      }
    },
    "manager": {
      "type": "ca-ai-chapter",
      "blocks": {
        "act_1": {
          "type": "act",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "After a release, something breaks and a customer finds it first.",
            "text": "<p>So every release is walked through the way a shopper would, on desktop and on a phone. A confirmed failure is rolled back.</p>",
            "length": 150
          }
        },
        "act_2": {
          "type": "act",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "The worst failures don't throw an error.",
            "text": "<p>A collection that quietly stops showing one product. A filter that returns the wrong ones. A checkout with no shipping rates. Each is checked again before anyone is told.</p>",
            "length": 150
          }
        },
        "act_3": {
          "type": "act",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "And it knows what never to touch.",
            "text": "<p>What was checked, what was caught and what became of it sit in one view.</p>",
            "length": 150,
            "never": "Pay for an order\nSubmit a real form\nSign in to your admin",
            "never_label": "Never"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "act_1",
        "act_2",
        "act_3"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "variant": "manager",
        "number": "02",
        "chapter": "The AI site manager"
      }
    },
    "healing": {
      "type": "ca-ai-chapter",
      "blocks": {
        "act_1": {
          "type": "act",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "The software behind your store breaks when nobody is watching.",
            "text": "<p>Here it is found first. Errors are picked up from the systems your orders depend on, not from a customer writing in.</p>",
            "length": 150
          }
        },
        "act_2": {
          "type": "act",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Diagnosed, fixed, reviewed and merged.",
            "text": "<p>A second reviewer reads every fix before it ships. People set the rules for what may merge on its own.</p>",
            "length": 150
          }
        },
        "act_3": {
          "type": "act",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Then verified, the same way a release is.",
            "text": "<p>Security moves at the same pace. When a critical vulnerability was announced in October, our own systems were patched the next day.</p>",
            "length": 150
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "act_1",
        "act_2",
        "act_3"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "variant": "healing",
        "number": "03",
        "chapter": "Self-healing software"
      }
    },
    "close": {
      "type": "ca-ai-chapter",
      "blocks": {
        "act_1": {
          "type": "act",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Know what is happening across your business, and have it handled.",
            "text": "<p>We set this up around your store, your team and your tools, then run it with you.</p>",
            "length": 170,
            "button_label": "Book a call",
            "button_link": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "act_1"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "variant": "close",
        "number": "",
        "chapter": ""
      }
    },
